course: dictionary
lesson: 11554
title: Amused: funny or busy?
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: The word amused has two main meanings. The first is finding something funny, so that you smile or laugh. «The puppy chased its own tail, and the children were amused.» The puppy is funny, so the children smile.
explain: The second meaning is kept busy and happy, not bored. «We packed cards and books to keep the little ones amused on the long train trip.» Nobody is laughing here. The children are busy and happy, so they are not bored.
explain: Watch for the phrase «not amused». It does not mean fun. It means someone is annoyed. «Dad was not amused when we spilled juice on the carpet.» Dad was cross, not smiling.
explain: Look at the words around amused to choose the right meaning. Words like laughed, smiled or joke point to funny. Words like trip, games or busy point to kept busy. Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
fact: Amused is an adjective. It is also the past form of the verb amuse.
fact: «Amused» means finding something funny, so that you smile or laugh.
fact: «Amused» can also mean kept busy and happy, not bored.
fact: The phrase «not amused» means annoyed, not happy.
fact: Amused is often followed by by or at, as in «amused by the joke».
exercise: «The puppy chased its tail, and the whole class looked amused.» What does amused mean here? | Lost in thought | Tired and ready for bed | Very angry about the noise | *Finding it funny, so smiling or laughing
exercise: «We played word games to keep the little ones amused on the bus.» What does amused mean here? | Pleased with a gift | Hungry and cross | Frightened of the dark | *Kept busy and happy, not bored
exercise: Mum read the note and said, «I am not amused.» What does not amused mean? | Excited about a trip | Asleep | *Annoyed | Very funny
test: «Grandma told a joke, and Tom was amused by it.» What does amused mean? | Frightened | *Finding it funny, so smiling | Annoyed and cross | Hungry for lunch
test: «The rainy day was long, so I drew pictures to stay amused.» What does amused mean? | Angry | Bored and sleepy | *Kept busy and happy, not bored | Wet through
exam: «When the teacher said, "I am not amused," the class went quiet.» What does not amused mean? | Very happy | Hungry for lunch | Surprised by a gift | *Annoyed
